We address the factorization of specific polynomial variants in the following two scenarios: 
(i) for certain Chebyshev polynomials expressed through the cosine function, where factors involve reduced 17th-degree polynomials; 
(ii) for a broader class of Chebyshev polynomial variants where factors consist of reduced 337th-degree polynomials and other elementary components.

